# Tabs

Use only `@/components/ui/tabs`. Do not add new tab bars, `FilterTabs`, segmented controls, or one-off button-group tabs.

## Visual pattern

Active = primary button. Inactive = outline button. Same look as Purchase Return status tabs.
In code this is the local `variant="button"` on Radian's `TabsList`; the `items` shortcut uses it for you.
`onValueChange` receives a `string`; narrow it when the state is a union type.

## Filter / status bar (no panels)

```tsx
import { Tabs, type TabItem } from "@/components/ui/tabs"

const items: TabItem[] = [
  { value: "approved", label: "Approved", count: 12 },
  { value: "draft", label: "Draft", count: 3 },
]

<Tabs items={items} value={value} onValueChange={setValue} />
```

## Module / content tabs (with panels)

```tsx
import { Tabs, TabsList, TabsTrigger, TabsContent } from "@/components/ui/tabs"

<Tabs value={value} onValueChange={setValue}>
  <TabsList variant="button">
    <TabsTrigger value="inventory">Inventory</TabsTrigger>
    <TabsTrigger value="purchase">Purchase</TabsTrigger>
  </TabsList>
  <TabsContent value="inventory">…</TabsContent>
  <TabsContent value="purchase">…</TabsContent>
</Tabs>
```

## Do not

- Import or recreate `filter-tabs`
- Use Radian's other `TabsList` variants (`default`, `open`, `ghost`) as a second style
- Build ad-hoc `ButtonGroup` + `Button` tablists for navigation/filtering
